<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV12"><note xml:lang="en">Though most of the items in this <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term> are found in the IAC, they are not included as a source or parallel. This is for purely practical reasons. Because of how the TNV and IAC are each organised, the only way to present the relevant sections of the IAC would be to list four enumerations for each poetic setting: trees, flowers, animals, and birds. The full enumerations are included in the commentary apparatus. Understand that they are also a parallel for the <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">mūlam</hi></term>.</note></standOff>
